Z||000000||2xsess||02-08-2001||09:48 PM||||I come here as a way to unwind and enjoy my favorite hobby, MY FIERO. It's really getting hard to relax here, everyone is bitching and fighting. I personally am getting rather tired of it. <BR>I see Vendors calling customers names and Fiero owners bad mouthing Vendors. If they make a shoddy product that's fine but why start a flame war with them? If they over charge ofr something then buy it else where or if you can't get it else where then I guess you really don't need/want it bad enough to pay their price. I'd love to have a Lambo ( a real one) but I don't email them and *****  about their prices. Doesn't make sense. I see posts all the time about The Fiero Stores prices but still a lot of members buy from them. I've even seen a few people unhappy with springs from them also but noones making threads titled "Fiero STore Sucks" and getting over 100 posts on it. So why does a thread by some MR2 owner (so he says) warrant like 60 posts in a day? I'm with PearlBlueSoul on this one, if you ignore him he'll go away. Or he'll just keep making stupid posts that noone reads, does that hurt our forum....I don't think so. But sitting there arguing with a "Faceless Typist" makes no sense to me. We all come here for fun, I think, at least that's why I come here. I know, someone will probably tell me that if I don't like it not to read the thread but I have to wonder why these threads get so many posts in such a short time. I really have enjoyed most of my experiences here but lately it's more stressful coming here than pulling a 14 hour day at work, and not getting paid over time   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> (sorry that's another gripe I have with the military) <BR>Also, until there's a spell check on the forum, who cares if someone can't spell 100%, I know there's a few members that have real grammar troubles but try to make the best of it, at least they don't come on here trying to talk trash about Fieros.(exception is when they misspell Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> )<P><B>All I'm trying to say is lighten up, these things don't directly impact your life. So why let them get you so riled up</B><P>Sorry, I had to do it, if you want to flame me then go ahead, I have an Army issue NOMEX suit.hehe.<P>Make Love not War   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">       <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>Visit My Website</A><p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 02-08-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000001||DrRodey||02-08-2001||09:57 PM||||I'll second everything Jeff just said...<P>------------------<BR>Hi... My names Dan, and i'm addicted to Fieros.<BR>'88 Formula CONVERTIBLE<BR>'85 Coupe<BR>AOL IM = drrodey<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/files/fieroPage.JPG">          <BR> <A HREF="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html" TARGET=_blank>freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fformula88||02-08-2001||10:05 PM||||Good call Jeff.  Maybe its a result of everyone getting tired of the bad weather.  Soon we can all pull our Fieros out of storage and take nice relaxing rides!  As for the "new members" like our recent MR2 guy, they start threads to get those responses.  They are people who enjoy upsetting groups and causing trouble.  60 posts an hour is what they want.  However, I can also understand people who post bak in defense of their Fiero.  The Fiero owners here love their car, and will defend it.  Peace!<P>------------------<BR>John<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">      <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2m6<BR>1987 Fiero Sport Coupe *In rebuilding*<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever2||02-08-2001||10:15 PM||||Point taken, and I agree, except that by posting it you are somewhat guilty of your own accusation.  But let's hope there will be little need for this kind of reminder.  <P>With as many opinions as there are members, this will never be considered a perfect site, but it's a good one or we wouldn't spend so much time here and it wouldn't be growing so fast.<P>I would say please use the same discretion here as you would face-to-face.  Disagreement is normal, even healthy in fact.  But decency, courtesy, and treating others the way you want to be treated is appreciated, although not required.  Just a good policy.  I'm probably not guiltless myself, so I'll step aside now and respectfully consider any other contributions to follow. ||||reg||6
